      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the development of aryl sulfones as Bradykinin B1 receptor antagonists. Variation of the linker region identified diol 23 as a potent B1 antagonist, while modifications of the aryl moiety led to compound 26, both of which were efficacious in rabbit biochemical challenge and pain models."},
